{
  "name": "earthworm",
  "_about": "The common earthworm (Lumbricus terrestris), 15 cm long and 7 mm thick: a long smooth ringed tube, pinkish brown, darker and redder at the front, the tail end flattened; the clitellum -- a thick orange-pink saddle over segments 32 to 37 -- a third of the way back; a blunt pointed head end. It creeps by waves of contraction running back down the body. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/soft.py on insectlib.py (one smooth body on a chain of bones that ripples as it crawls).",
